EXT. STALLED CABLE CAR OVER A GORGE - DAY

Wind. A steel box swaying under a single cable. Far below, a river like a thread.

JUNIPER, 30s, hiking boots, a torn pack, sits wedged against the door. She stares at the hatch in the ceiling. Her knuckles are white.

JUNIPER
(to the empty car)
Okay. Okay. Everyone stay calm.

No one answers. The car creaks.

JUNIPER (CONT'D)
(to herself)
You are not stuck. You are paused.

She reaches into her pack. Pulls a radio. Presses the button. Static.

JUNIPER (CONT'D)
(into radio)
Base, this is car nine. Anyone?

Static. She tries again. And again.

A bolt shears off somewhere above. Metal rings. The car lurches six inches. Juniper screams, clamps both hands on the rail.

JUNIPER (CONT'D)
(to the car)
No. No no no.

She closes her eyes. Breathes. In. Out.

She opens the hatch release. Pushes. Nothing. Pushes again. The latch squeals.

A shadow falls across the hatch.

BASHIR, 30s, in a climbing harness and a bright orange helmet, drops through the opening on a rope, boots first. He lands, steadies the car with one knee, and clips a carabiner to her pack.

BASHIR
Juniper?

JUNIPER
Who are you?

BASHIR
Rescue. They said you were alone.

JUNIPER
I was talking to the car.

BASHIR
How's the car?

JUNIPER
(laughs, shaky)
Needy.

He tightens the straps across her chest, one at a time, steady.

BASHIR
I'm going to lift you through the hatch. You look up, not down.

JUNIPER
Up. Not down.

BASHIR
Good.

He lifts. She rises into daylight, boots dangling.

JUNIPER
(from above)
I can see the sun!

BASHIR
Told you.

The car groans. He follows, last out. The cable hums.
